            <div xml:id="d585">

                <pb facs="0740" n="626" xml:id="pg626"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2814: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Commissioner in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-04-07T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 7, 1924—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. Your 23, March 25, 9 a.m. Department informed by Secretary of the Navy that
                    he has decided to keep General Lee in his office as Military Governor until
                    after July 1, and has therefore directed that the order for his relief in April
                    be revoked.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
